Output shell completions

Writes a completion script for SHELL to stdout.

If your shell already initializes completion, add only the source line after
that initialization. Completions are generated at shell startup. Open a new
shell to load the setup.

For zsh, add this to ~/.zshrc:
  autoload -Uz compinit
  compinit
  source <(snouty completions zsh)

For bash:
  snouty completions bash | sudo tee /etc/bash_completion.d/snouty

Usage: snouty completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          Shell to generate completions for
          
          [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
